# Code-signing credentials for `npm run tauri:build:mac` (local) and CI.
# Copy this file to `.env.signing` and fill in real values. `.env.signing` is gitignored.
#
# Pull these from the same Apple Developer account used by the VSCodium fork.
# Cert type required: "Developer ID Application" (NOT "Apple Development").
# Create one at https://developer.apple.com/account/resources/certificates if missing.

# ---- macOS ----

# Common name of the cert in Keychain. Run `security find-identity -v -p codesigning`
# and copy the quoted string for the "Developer ID Application: ..." row.
APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAMID)"

# Apple ID email used to log into developer.apple.com.
APPLE_ID="you@example.com"

# App-specific password (NOT your Apple ID password).
# Generate at https://appleid.apple.com → Sign-In and Security → App-Specific Passwords.
APPLE_PASSWORD="xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx"

# 10-char Team ID. Find it at https://developer.apple.com/account → Membership.
APPLE_TEAM_ID="ABCDE12345"

# ---- Tauri updater (optional, only needed if shipping updates) ----
# Generate once with: npx @tauri-apps/cli signer generate -w ~/.tauri/codex-updater.key
# Then paste the contents of the .key file (single line, base64) here.
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=""
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=""
